From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:56:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xgameruntime: Implement XUser through the Xodus service.

Sign-in: XUserAddAsync() gets the user's and the device's RPS tickets for the title's MSA app
from the Xodus service and signs in as Win32 titles do, through SISU: a device token from
device.auth.xboxlive.com, then the user, title and XSTS tokens from sisu.xboxlive.com/authorize,
all bound to an ECDSA P-256 proof key with which the requests are signed. The user's xuid,
gamertags, age group and privileges come from the XSTS claims. One user is signed in at a time;
adding again returns it, and with no account in the service XUserAddAsync() fails with
E_GAMEUSER_NO_DEFAULT_USER.

Tokens: XUserGetTokenAndSignature() follows the NSAL, the title's endpoint list then the default
one, the most specific entry winning; WebSocket URLs are looked up as their HTTP counterparts. A
URL with no relying party gets E_GAMEUSER_NO_TOKEN_REQUIRED, which XSAPI takes as "send no
Authorization header". XSTS tokens are cached per relying party until five minutes before they
expire and renewed once from new tickets on a 401; a relying party that refuses one, or a failed
renewal of the user's tokens, is not tried again for a minute. Requests are signed when their
endpoint has a signature policy, as the GDK documentation's "Proof keys" section describes
(version 1, ES256); results follow Xal's documentation (sizes count the NUL, an unsigned request
has a null signature).

Requests go through WinHTTP, which validates certificates, with a failed GET tried once more;
JSON goes through Windows.Data.Json. Failures log the host, the HTTP status and XErr, never a
token. Gamer pictures, ResolveIssue, adding a user by id, sign-out and MSA tokens for the title
are stubs.

NsalTests check URL parsing, endpoint matching and the signed bytes offline. XUserNoAccountTests
need a service with no account (XGR_XODUS_NO_ACCOUNT=1), and XUserLiveTests sign in for real
(XGR_LIVE_XBOX=1, a signed-in service and the title's MicrosoftGame.config).

Written anew after WineGDK's XUser.c (LGPL-2.1-or-later), Microsoft's documentation and the Xal
headers; original work for macrock.

Topic: xuser
